    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17032" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">expĕtesso</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-isso</span></b> ),
		ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. intens. a.</i> [id.], <i>to
			desire</i>, <i>long for</i> (a Plautinian word): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae te amat tuamque expetessit pulcram
					pulcritudinem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 4, 1, 13</span></i>
			: cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 6, 14</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Trin. 2, 1, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Rud. 1, 5, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ultro amas, ultro expetessis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 3, 1, 23</span></i>
			.</div>
